<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n70333" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">νεό-πλουτος</span></b> , <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ον</span>,
			<div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>A.</b><i>newly become rich,</i>
			opp. <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἀρχαιόπλουτος</span> (q.v.): hence,
				<i>vainglorious, upstart,</i>
			<i><span class="en">
				D.
				17.23
			</span></i>, cf. Arg.<i><span class="en">
				D.
				17
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				Arist.
				<u>Rh.</u>
				1387a23
			</span></i>; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">οἰκέτης ν.</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Luc.
					<u>Hist.Conscr.</u>
					20
				</span></i>
			; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἀπελεύθερος ν.</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Plu.
					2.634c
				</span></i>
			; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ν. δεῖπνα</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Id.
					<u>Luc.</u>
					40
				</span></i>
			: hence, by a comic metaph., <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ν.
			τρύξ,</span> of a low <i>upstart,</i>
			<i><span class="en">
				Ar.
				<u>V.</u>
				1309
			</span></i>.</div>
